From 0bcfeca441a011e84b8823522cdda31a0e3d158d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mitgor <mitgor@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:45:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: add a bounded DSP-only DF17 rescue replay prototype

Add an opt-in reference tool for comparing clipped energy slicing,
fractional timing retries, bounded weak-bit correction and preamble-derived
matched filtering against a paired readsb replay.

Keep native kernels isolated from the normal readsb build. Require a verified
shared RF clock, stock-only prior identity, CRC validity and conservative
transmission deduplication before counting provisional additions. The tool
writes local JSON only; no SDR ownership, feeder output, learned components
or service configuration is included.

Include independent numerical references, guard/boundary tests, a native
ASan/UBSan harness and limited paired replay results. This proposal is an
offline contrib prototype; native live-demodulator integration remains a
separate design/review step.
